= The Cheka

On 20 December Sovnarkom created the All-Russian Extraordinary Commission for the Struggle against Counter-Revolution and Sabotage. Its chairman is Felix Dzerzhinsky, a Pole and a former prison inmate of the tsar. The Left SRs have asked for seats on its board; four of them will have them in January.

The new commission has the power to arrest, to investigate and, in some cases, to decide. It appeared in a country that has not yet got a legal system, and that has abolished the tsar's.

- @steinberg: Campaign with the Left SR Commissar of Justice, Isaac Steinberg.
- @ignore: Say nothing. It is too soon to tell.
- @denounce: Denounce it.

@steinberg
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 5, repression: -2, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, -1);
Q.steinberg_line = 1;
!}

We joined Steinberg's campaign for revolutionary legality: no arrests without a warrant, no executions without a trial. It did not stop the Cheka, but it embarrassed it.

@ignore
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 2);
!}

The party made no statement. Our comrades will be among its first customers.

@denounce
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -3, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {middle: 2, workers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 1, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, -2);
!}

[? if player_party = 'menshevik' : Our press ?][? if player_party = 'sr' : The party's press ?] called the commission a revival of the Okhrana, and the paper was banned for a week.
